# <type>[(<scope>)][!]: <subject>   (50 chars max, imperative mood)
#
# <body>   (72 chars wrap; explain WHY, not WHAT — the diff shows what)
#
# <footer>   (optional: BREAKING CHANGE:, Refs: #123, Closes: #456)
#
# ── Types ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   feat      new capability
#   fix       bug fix
#   chore     tooling, deps, non-functional
#   docs      documentation only
#   refactor  rearrangement with no behavior change
#   test      adding / correcting tests
#   perf      performance improvement
#   build     build system, compilation, packaging
#   ci        CI/CD config
#   style     formatting, whitespace (no logic)
#   revert    revert a previous commit
#
# Add `!` after type/scope for breaking changes (e.g. `feat!:` or `feat(api)!:`).
# Scope is optional; use a short noun identifying the subsystem (`api`, `cli`, `auth`).
